<section class="style-guide-section">
  <h2>Reference Pairing</h2>
  <p>This sample borrows the feel of fLaMEd Fury's pairing: <strong>Yanoneka</strong> for display, a plain <strong>system sans</strong> for body copy, and a clipped gradient title using your existing green palette.</p>

  <article class="post-item style-guide-entry-sample style-guide-flamed-sample preview-body-system">
    <header>
      <h2 class="post-title preview-title-yanoneka style-guide-gradient-title">
        <a href="#">A green flame title without leaving your palette</a>
      </h2>
      <div class="post-meta">
        <time datetime="2026-04-07">April 7, 2026</time>
        <span class="post-tags">
          <a href="#">#yanoneka</a>, <a href="#">#system-ui</a>, <a href="#">#gradient</a>
        </span>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="post-content">
      <p>The trick is just text clipping: make the title text transparent, give it a gradient background, and clip that background to the glyph shapes. The display face does most of the personality work.</p>
      <p>This keeps the surrounding page in your current colors while letting the headline feel brighter and more alive than the solid green title bars elsewhere on the site.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</section>

