<section class="style-guide-section">
  <h2>Text Elements</h2>
  <p>This is a normal paragraph using the live body style. It should read cleanly on the dark moss panel and still feel soft against the green shell of the page.</p>
  <p>This paragraph also includes <a href="#">a normal link</a>, <strong>strong text</strong>, <em>emphasized text</em>, and <code>inline code</code> to show how mixed inline formatting behaves.</p>

  <p><abbr title="Application Programming Interface">API</abbr> abbreviations, <mark>highlighted text</mark>, and keyboard-style inline examples like <code>Ctrl + Shift + P</code> are worth checking too.</p>

  <blockquote>
    <p>This is the current blockquote style with the green left rail. It is useful for checking how softer emphasis elements feel beside the larger body text.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <ol>
    <li>A numbered list item using the live spacing.</li>
    <li>A second item to compare against bullets.</li>
  </ol>

  <ul>
    <li>A bulleted list item using the live spacing.</li>
    <li>Another item for checking rhythm and legibility.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr>

  <details>
    <summary>Details and summary element</summary>
    <p>This is useful for checking disclosure styling when it appears inside long-form posts or notes.</p>
  </details>
</section>

